WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:16.436
Nan was exceptionally brave, she was afraid of a bear in the dark woods.

2
00:00:18.357 --> 00:00:21.258
That is, until the bear mooed.

3
00:00:26.001 --> 00:00:29.223
When she heard the sound, Nan laughed with relief.

4
00:00:29.243 --> 00:00:33.937
"Oh, Rob, that's not a bear—that's a cow!"

5
00:00:39.618 --> 00:00:43.019
The two children petted the cow until it wandered away.

6
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:50.001
Nan wanted to resume searching for their friends, but Rob refused to walk.

7
00:00:50.021 --> 00:00:54.962
"It's nighttime and I'm sleepy and I want Mama!"

8
00:00:55.322 --> 00:00:56.403
the little boy said.

9
00:00:56.423 --> 00:01:00.584
"Maybe you need a nap," Nan replied.

10
00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:06.793
"Let's sit down, and you can rest your head on my lap."

11
00:01:06.813 --> 00:01:14.196
"Wake me when Mama comes," Rob said, and soon he was asleep.

12
00:01:16.037 --> 00:01:21.339
Nan sat anxiously, hoping that no more animals would emerge from the darkness.

13
00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.761
By the time the moon rose, she too had fallen asleep.

14
00:01:28.142 --> 00:01:32.904
While Nan and Rob slept, everyone at Plumfield was in a state of panic.

15
00:01:34.476 --> 00:01:41.139
Dan, Demi, and Daisy had traveled home in the cart with Silas while the other boys had decided

16
00:01:41.179 --> 00:01:41.899
to walk home.

17
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.462
When Nat, Tommy, and Jack finally showed up, Jo flew out of her chair.

18
00:01:48.482 --> 00:01:50.703
"Where are Nan and Rob?"

19
00:01:51.023 --> 00:01:51.724
she demanded.

20
00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:56.306
"We thought they rode home with Dan and the twins," Nat said.

21
00:01:56.326 --> 00:01:59.807
"We thought you knew where they were!"

22
00:02:00.248 --> 00:02:00.968
Demi said.

23
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.101
Now it was Jo's turn to be frightened.

24
00:02:05.121 --> 00:02:06.822
"Find Mr.

25
00:02:06.842 --> 00:02:07.802
Bauer and Silas!"

26
00:02:08.402 --> 00:02:09.003
she cried.

27
00:02:09.023 --> 00:02:13.905
"Fetch the lanterns, and Jack and Nat, come with me!"

28
00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:19.607
Soon the professor and Silas were on their way to the big pasture.

29
00:02:20.827 --> 00:02:24.989
Without bothering to put on her shawl, Jo rode away on Toby.

30
00:02:25.009 --> 00:02:27.110
"Wait for me!"

31
00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:28.991
a voice cried behind her.

32
00:02:30.851 --> 00:02:35.538
As Jo turned around, her lantern revealed Dan hurrying down the drive.

33
00:02:35.558 --> 00:02:38.259
"What are you doing here?"

34
00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.320
she asked.

35
00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.561
"And where are Jack and Nat?"

36
00:02:41.581 --> 00:02:46.944
"I told them I'd accompany you because they hadn't eaten any supper yet," Dan said.

37
00:02:46.964 --> 00:02:50.906
"Besides, I wanted to come more than they did."

38
00:02:50.926 --> 00:02:59.151
"If you insist on helping, then you have to ride Toby," Jo said, jumping off the donkey and

39
00:02:59.231 --> 00:03:00.672
handing the reins to Dan.

40
00:03:01.964 --> 00:03:03.385
But Dan wouldn't take them.

41
00:03:03.405 --> 00:03:12.230
"I couldn't, ma'am," he said, "because you—" "You're no use to us if you make your foot worse

42
00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.091
with too much walking," Jo reminded him.

43
00:03:16.632 --> 00:03:22.095
Reluctantly Dan climbed onto Toby and set off with Jo walking beside him.

44
00:03:26.318 --> 00:03:32.993
Rob!" Periodically they stopped and called for the children, but no little voices replied.

45
00:03:34.994 --> 00:03:39.416
When they arrived at the big pasture, they saw lanterns flitting here and there.

46
00:03:40.997 --> 00:03:43.458
The professor shouted, "Nan!

47
00:03:44.158 --> 00:03:47.379
Rob! Rob!

48
00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:52.982
Nan!" while Silas whistled and yelled.

49
00:03:53.002 --> 00:03:54.743
"Hush, everyone!"

50
00:03:55.223 --> 00:03:57.604
Jo said with a sob in her voice.

51
00:03:58.808 --> 00:04:01.310
"You're frightening them with all this noise.

52
00:04:02.691 --> 00:04:06.033
Rob will recognize my voice, so let me call.

53
00:04:10.496 --> 00:04:15.580
Rob!" Over and over she called with no response.

54
00:04:17.221 --> 00:04:23.326
The sky was overcast now, and the moon made only brief appearances from behind the clouds.

55
00:04:24.586 --> 00:04:29.506
A far-off rumble of thunder indicated that a summer storm was brewing.

56
00:04:30.846 --> 00:04:33.928
Jo wandered through the field like a pale ghost.

57
00:04:33.948 --> 00:04:37.190
"Oh, my poor Rob!

58
00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:42.153
And if Nan's been harmed, how will I ever explain it to her father?

59
00:04:43.473 --> 00:04:45.234
Oh, Rob, where are you?"

60
00:04:47.156 --> 00:04:50.497
Dan could not take Jo's despair for another moment.

61
00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:54.680
He dismounted and tied Toby to a fence.

62
00:04:56.836 --> 00:04:59.078
"Maybe they went into the woods," he said.

63
00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:03.622
Then he climbed over the wall before Jo could stop him.

64
00:05:03.642 --> 00:05:06.084
"I see footprints!"

65
00:05:06.464 --> 00:05:07.685
he cried a moment later.

66
00:05:07.705 --> 00:05:09.046
"Come here!"

67
00:05:10.908 --> 00:05:14.991
Jo was the first to reach Dan, who was shining a lantern on the ground.

68
00:05:15.011 --> 00:05:19.034
"Yes!" she cried joyfully.

69
00:05:19.054 --> 00:05:21.917
"Those are tracks from Rob's boots!"

70
00:05:24.539 --> 00:05:31.213
A little farther on, they found Nan's hat, and they soon came upon the two children, both sound

71
00:05:31.253 --> 00:05:33.914
asleep. "Rob!"

72
00:05:34.494 --> 00:05:37.395
Jo cried, sweeping him into her arms.

73
00:05:38.936 --> 00:05:40.736
"Mama! I knew you'd come!"

74
00:05:44.037 --> 00:05:47.278
Rob clutched his pail of berries, which was still full.

75
00:05:47.298 --> 00:05:50.639
"Look at all the berries I picked for you!"

76
00:05:52.259 --> 00:05:56.509
Meanwhile Dan gently picked up Nan, who began to cry.

77
00:06:03.094 --> 00:06:05.396
poor little girl, don't cry!"

78
00:06:05.916 --> 00:06:06.557
Jo said.

79
00:06:06.577 --> 00:06:11.861
"You're safe now, and we won't ask for any explanations tonight."

80
00:06:13.082 --> 00:06:15.584
But Nan's apology came tumbling out.

81
00:06:16.292 --> 00:06:17.493
"It's all my fault.

82
00:06:18.134 --> 00:06:22.858
I tried my best to take care of Rob, and I let him sleep, and I didn't eat

83
00:06:22.958 --> 00:06:25.900
any of his berries, even though I was so hungry.

84
00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:34.287
I'll never do it again, I promise and She dissolved in tears, relieved to be rescued.

85
00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:39.992
After a happy reunion with the professor and Silas, the group set out for home.

86
00:06:42.194 --> 00:06:46.693
Daisy and the boys were still awake, and they joyfully greeted Rob and Nan.

87
00:06:46.713 --> 00:06:54.996
"It's almost 11 o'clock," the professor said when the wanderers had finished a late supper.

88
00:06:55.016 --> 00:06:57.638
"Time for bed, everyone."

89
00:06:57.658 --> 00:07:05.941
"Thank goodness there won't be any empty beds tonight," Jo said, her eyes filling with tears.

90
00:07:07.782 --> 00:07:12.484
While Daisy escorted Nan to bed, the professor carried Rob upstairs.

91
00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:22.042
"Poor Aunt Jo is so tired, she should be carried upstairs too," Demi said.

92
00:07:22.062 --> 00:07:24.523
"Let's do that!"

93
00:07:24.683 --> 00:07:25.584
Tommy shouted.

94
00:07:25.604 --> 00:07:28.025
"No, thank you!"

95
00:07:28.485 --> 00:07:31.086
Jo said, fearing Tommy might drop her.

96
00:07:31.106 --> 00:07:35.068
"But someone may lend me an arm to lean on."

97
00:07:35.088 --> 00:07:38.309
"Me! Me!

98
00:07:38.369 --> 00:07:41.890
Me!" The boys jostled each other, eager to be chosen.

99
00:07:43.551 --> 00:07:49.191
Jo smiled at Dan and said, "You found the children, so you must be given the honor."

100
00:07:51.673 --> 00:07:54.055
Dan proudly escorted her upstairs.

101
00:07:55.937 --> 00:08:01.021
When they reached Jo's door, she turned and said, "God bless you, my boy."

102
00:08:02.262 --> 00:08:07.406
Dan hesitated and then said softly, "I wish I really were your boy."

103
00:08:07.426 --> 00:08:13.912
"I will always think of you as my oldest son," Jo said, kissing his cheek.

104
00:08:15.605 --> 00:08:19.143
And that was more than enough to satisfy Dan.
